---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { entity } from "../data/entity";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Global Book Publishing collects, uses, and protects the information you share with us through forms, calls, and email."
>
  <section class="bg-navy-900 text-offwhite-100">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">LEGAL</p>
      <h1 class="on-navy">Privacy Policy</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-ivory-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 leading-relaxed">
      <div class="card p-5 border-dashed bg-gold-100 border-gold-500 mb-10">
        <p class="font-semibold">
          This is a draft starting point. Have a lawyer review this page before it governs real
          transactions. [NEEDS CONFIRMATION: legal review]
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-8">Last updated: [NEEDS CONFIRMATION: publish date]</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We collect what you give us, directly, through the forms on this site: your name, email address, and
        answers to questions like your profession or where you are in your book (for example, when you
        request the Expert Book Blueprint, book a strategy call, or subscribe to the newsletter). We don't
        collect information you didn't hand us on purpose.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">How we use it</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We use this information to send you what you asked for (a guide, a booking confirmation, a
        newsletter), to reach out if you've asked us to, and to understand which pages and offers are
        actually useful to the people who visit this site. We tag your information by profession and journey
        stage so the emails you get are relevant instead of generic.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">What we don't do</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We do not sell your personal information to anyone. We do not share it with third parties for their
        own marketing purposes. If that ever changes, this page will say so, plainly, before it happens.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        This site may use basic analytics tools to understand traffic and page performance (for example,
        which articles get read and which forms get completed). [NEEDS CONFIRMATION: exact analytics
        provider(s) in use and their own data retention policies]. You can control cookies through your
        browser settings at any time.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Where your data is stored</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Form submissions are sent to our CRM and email systems so we can respond to you and send the
        resources you requested. [NEEDS CONFIRMATION: specific CRM/email provider name(s) for a fully
        accurate disclosure].
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        You can ask us what information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. You
        can unsubscribe from any email at any time using the link in that email, no questions asked.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">How to reach us about your data</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Contact us at {entity.contactEmail || "[NEEDS CONFIRMATION: legal contact email]"} with any privacy
        question or request. You can also reach us through the <a href="/contact" class="underline font-semibold">contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        If this policy changes in a material way, we'll update the date at the top of this page. Continued
        use of the site after a change means you've accepted the update.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
